{"units": [{"id": "dysmoros-quote2", "translation": "grievously"}, {"id": "dysmoros-quote3", "translation": "ill-fated"}, {"id": "dysodopaipalos-orth1", "translation": "pathless and rugged"}, {"id": "dysodopaipalos-def1", "translation": "pathless and rugged"}, {"id": "dysodopaipalos-note1", "translation": "Improperly"}, {"id": "dysodopaipalos-note2", "translation": "which the scholiast explains as δυσπαράβατα καὶ τραχέα ζῶσι καὶ τοῖς θνήσκουσι [hard to traverse and rough for the living and the dying],"}, {"id": "dysodopaipalos-quote1", "translation": "allotments pathless and rugged for those who see and for the blind alike."}, {"id": "dysodopaipalos-quote2", "translation": "hard to traverse and rough for the living and the dying"}, {"id": "dysoizo-orth1", "translation": "to fear"}, {"id": "dysoizo-def1", "translation": "to fear"}, {"id": "dysoizo-note1", "translation": "Hesychius explains it by φοβεῖσθαι [to fear], ὑπονοεῖν [to suspect], δυσχεραίνειν [to be distressed]. The middle form δυσοίζου [you fear] is used by the author of Rhesus 805."}, {"id": "dysoizo-quote1", "translation": "I do not fear, like a bird in a bush, out of terror."}, {"id": "dysoizo-quote2", "translation": "to fear"}, {"id": "dysoizo-quote3", "translation": "to suspect"}, {"id": "dysoizo-quote4", "translation": "to be distressed"}, {"id": "dysoizo-quote5", "translation": "you fear"}, {"id": "dysoimos-orth1", "translation": "having a bad road"}, {"id": "dysoimos-def1", "translation": "having a bad road"}, {"id": "dysoimos-quote1", "translation": "of an ill-omened fortune."}, {"id": "dysoistos-orth1", "translation": "hard to bear"}, {"id": "dysoistos-def1", "translation": "hard to bear"}, {"id": "dysoistos-quote1", "translation": "sufferings hard to look upon and hard to bear."}, {"id": "dysoistos-quote2", "translation": "pains hard to bear."}, {"id": "dysoistos-quote3", "translation": "I suffered things hard to bear for the citizens."}, {"id": "dysomilos-orth1", "translation": "hard to associate with, difficult to converse with"}, {"id": "dysomilos-def1", "translation": "one with whom it is difficult to have dealings, hard to address"}, {"id": "dysomilos-quote1", "translation": "restless and hard to associate with."}, {"id": "dysommatos-orth1", "translation": "blind"}, {"id": "dysommatos-def1", "translation": "blind"}, {"id": "dysommatos-quote1", "translation": "for those who see and for the blind alike."}, {"id": "dysormos-orth1", "translation": "without a harbor"}, {"id": "dysormos-def1", "translation": "without a harbor"}, {"id": "dysormos-def2", "translation": "Of adverse winds keeping ships in harbor"}, {"id": "dysormos-quote1", "translation": "an island — small, without a harbor for ships."}, {"id": "dysormos-quote2", "translation": "winds — idle, fasting, without a harbor."}, {"id": "dysornis-orth1", "translation": "of ill omen"}, {"id": "dysornis-def1", "translation": "of ill omen"}, {"id": "dysornis-quote1", "translation": "this ill-omened concert of the spear."}, {"id": "dyspalaistos-orth1", "translation": "hard to wrestle with, invincible"}, {"id": "dyspalaistos-def1", "translation": "hard to wrestle with, invincible"}, {"id": "dyspalaistos-quote1", "translation": "O curse of this house, hard to wrestle with."}, {"id": "dyspalaistos-quote2", "translation": "matters hard to wrestle with."}, {"id": "dyspalamos-orth1", "translation": "hard to overcome"}, {"id": "dyspalamos-def1", "translation": "hard to overcome"}, {"id": "dyspalamos-quote1", "translation": "the gods' hard-to-overcome — wiles."}, {"id": "dyspalamos_adv-orth1", "translation": "helplessly, in desperate plight"}, {"id": "dyspalamos_adv-def1", "translation": "without help, with no hope of safety"}, {"id": "dyspalamos_adv-quote1", "translation": "may you perish helplessly."}, {"id": "dyspales-orth1", "translation": "hard to wrestle with, hard to overcome"}, {"id": "dyspales-def1", "translation": "not easily wrestled with, hard to overcome"}, {"id": "dyspales-quote1", "translation": "in the midst of a whirlpool hard to wrestle with."}, {"id": "dysparaboulos-orth1", "translation": "hard to persuade"}, {"id": "dysparaboulos-def1", "translation": "one who is hard to persuade"}, {"id": "dysparaboulos-quote1", "translation": "with minds hard to persuade."}, {"id": "dysparathelktos-orth1", "translation": "hard to move"}, {"id": "dysparathelktos-def1", "translation": "one who is hard to move"}, {"id": "dysparathelktos-note1", "translation": "Thus Schuetz for ὦ δυσπαρθέλκτοις [O hard-to-move] (δυσπαραθέλκτοις [hard-to-move] Robortellus) παθόντος οἴκτοις [by the pities of the sufferer], which is in M, with δυσπαρθενήτοις [hard-to-move] written in the margin."}, {"id": "dysparathelktos-quote1", "translation": "the wrath of Zeus, protector of suppliants, remains hard to move by the pities of the sufferer."}, {"id": "dysparathelktos-quote2", "translation": "O hard-to-move (hard-to-move Robortellus) by the pities of the sufferer"}, {"id": "dysparathelktos-quote3", "translation": "hard-to-move"}, {"id": "dysparaitetos-orth1", "translation": "inexorable"}, {"id": "dysparaitetos-def1", "translation": "inexorable"}, {"id": "dysparaitetos-quote1", "translation": "for the mind of Zeus is inexorable."}, {"id": "dysparegoros-orth1", "translation": "hard to appease"}, {"id": "dysparegoros-def1", "translation": "hard to appease"}, {"id": "dysparegoros-note1", "translation": "Scholiast: οὐ ταχέως παρηγορούμεναι ὑπὸ βροτῶν [not quickly appeased by mortals]."}, {"id": "dysparegoros-quote1", "translation": "hard to appease by mortals."}, {"id": "dysparegoros-quote2", "translation": "not quickly appeased by mortals"}, {"id": "dyspemptos-orth1", "translation": "hard to send away"}, {"id": "dyspemptos-def1", "translation": "hard to send away"}, {"id": "dyspemptos-quote1", "translation": "hard to send away."}, {"id": "dyspetos-orth1", "translation": "with difficulty"}, {"id": "dyspetos-def1", "translation": "with difficulty"}, {"id": "dyspetos-quote1", "translation": "you would bear my toils with difficulty."}, {"id": "dysplanos-orth1", "translation": "wandering miserably"}, {"id": "dysplanos-def1", "translation": "wandering miserably"}, {"id": "dysplanos-quote1", "translation": "tell the maiden who wanders miserably."}, {"id": "dysplanos-quote2", "translation": "in the wanderings of Hera that cause miserable wandering."}, {"id": "dyspolemetos-orth1", "translation": "hard to conquer in war"}, {"id": "dyspolemetos-def1", "translation": "hard to conquer in war"}, {"id": "dyspolemetos-note1", "translation": "δυσπόλεμον [hard to conquer], which Butler,"}, {"id": "dyspolemetos-quote1", "translation": "having seen the divine avenger and the hard-to-conquer scout."}, {"id": "dyspolemetos-quote2", "translation": "hard to conquer, which"}, {"id": "dyspolemos-orth1", "translation": "unfortunate in war"}, {"id": "dyspolemos-def1", "translation": "unfortunate in war"}, {"id": "dyspolemos-quote1", "translation": "the race of the Persians is unfortunate in war."}, {"id": "dysponetos-orth1", "translation": "causing toil"}, {"id": "dysponetos-def1", "translation": "causing toil"}, {"id": "dysponetos-note1", "translation": "Scholiast: δυστυχίας αἴτιε [cause of misfortune]."}, {"id": "dysponetos-note2", "translation": "Another example of this word is in Sophocles, Oedipus at Colonus 1614, where Oedipus says to his daughters κοὐκέτι τὴν δυσπόνητον ἕξετ᾽ ἀμφ᾿ ἐμοὶ τροφήν [and no longer will you have the toilsome care of me], where the scholiast correctly understands τὴν γηροκομίαν [the tending of old age]."}, {"id": "dysponetos-quote1", "translation": "O toil-causing divinity."}, {"id": "dysponetos-quote2", "translation": "cause of misfortune"}, {"id": "dysponetos-quote3", "translation": "and no longer will you have the toilsome care of me"}, {"id": "dysponetos-quote4", "translation": "the tending of old age"}, {"id": "dyspotmos-orth1", "translation": "ill-fated, unhappy"}, {"id": "dyspotmos-def1", "translation": "ill-fated, unhappy"}, {"id": "dyspotmos-quote1", "translation": "you see me, a god, imprisoned and ill-fated."}, {"id": "dyspotmos-quote2", "translation": "and everywhere ill-fated things."}, {"id": "dyspotmos-quote3", "translation": "an ill-fated race."}, {"id": "dyspotmos-quote4", "translation": "borne along according to the ill-fated prayers of my father."}]}